      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "term=143\nhup=129\n",
        "stderr": ""
      },
      "note": "bash reports a child a signal ended as 128 plus it, and a managed runner's cancellation carries the signal kill named; INT and QUIT are left out, since a non-interactive bash's asynchronous commands may ignore them."
